//RS /// Folds single-use temporaries into their consumer. `out[slots_start..
//RS /// slots_end]` holds the function's slot declarations and everything after
//RS /// it the body. A body slot defined as `Some(E)` from a pure expression `E`
//RS /// and read once, by the next statement of the same straight-line run (only
//RS /// pure definitions between), as a clone or take of the slot, takes `(E)` in
//RS /// place of that read when nothing else in the consumer or in between names a
//RS /// variable of `E` (an assignment target local excepted, since the right side
//RS /// runs first) and the read is not inside a closure. A hoisted slot defined
//RS /// by a borrowing closure carrier (`borrowing_closure_expression`) folds the
//RS /// same way, as a block typed like the slot. The definition and its top
